Writing is EXPERIMENTAL. Make sure you have a backup of your important files.
• The disk is checked first; if a problem is found, writing is not enabled. • Always use "Safely eject" before removing the disk or plugging it into a Mac. • Files deleted on this disk do not go to the Recycle Bin; they are deleted permanently. • You can choose "Back to read-only" at any time; your changes are saved.
